& [DerivedIR4FinalSlicesSource] is the preserved source record for minting IR4 final slices
  + [source_kind] is derived_boundary_source
  + [source_basis] is accepted post-FSC5 readiness surface, accepted FSC3 runtime graph proof pack, and accepted IR3 operator harness implementation proof pack
  + [target_chunk] is IR4 LangGraph proof runtime implementation
  + [target_chunk_state] is ready_for_final_slice_minting_after_IR3_completion
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is LangGraph runtime integration, checkpoint semantics, SOP-first interrupt behavior, and operator-trace proof boundaries affect authority/projection handoff

  = must: mint IR4 final slices before creating executable LangGraph runtime code
  = must: keep LangGraph checkpoints and graph state as execution state only
  = must: use IR3 operator harness proof as the accepted execution/operator boundary input
  = must: preserve SOP-first interrupt for ambiguous identity, authority conflict, stale input, missing proof route, contested coordination claim, high-risk operation, human override, unsupported scope, and checkpoint authority confusion
  = must: require operator_trace or equivalent trace evidence for every runtime path before future surfaces consume it
  = must: keep generated runtime checkpoints, generated traces, generated reports, and fixture outputs projection-only
  - never: authorize operations control, live machine control, job dispatch, process control, GPU control, network control, credential access, destructive filesystem action, or hidden source mutation

& [IR4SliceIntentSet] is the intended whole-pie slice shape for IR4
  + [slice_intent] is import and reconcile FSC3 runtime graph contracts with IR3 operator harness implementation proof
  + [slice_intent] is define the bounded LangGraph proof runtime implementation contract without installing dependencies or writing executable graph code
  + [slice_intent] is define checkpoint persistence and resume policy as non-authoritative generated execution state
  + [slice_intent] is define SOP-first interrupt fixture and expected-ledger material for graph execution
  + [slice_intent] is define runtime trace and completion-gate fixture material for success, blocked, stale, fault, and interrupt outcomes
  + [slice_intent] is produce implementation activation pack only after contract, checkpoint, fixture, and trace proof surfaces are accepted

& [IR4ForbiddenScopeSet] is the forbidden scope for IR4 final-slice minting
  + [forbidden_scope] is executable LangGraph node implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is dependency installation
  + [forbidden_scope] is checkpoint persistence implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is surface or adapter implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is operations simulator implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is operations control
  + [forbidden_scope] is live machine control

& [IR4DownstreamGate] is the downstream state after IR4 final slices are minted
  + [first_slice_after_minting] is IR4-S01 runtime boundary import and invariant reconciliation
  + [downstream_chunk] is IR5 surface projection prototype remains gated until IR4 proof is accepted
  + [future_spark_suitable_work] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after IR4 contracts, fixtures, and activation boundaries isolate bounded implementation
